--- A function handed a record at one call and an int at another holds a
--- record or none (spec: 0 is none, another int stops), and arithmetic on
--- what it answers is refused naming it so, with the way out: the message
--- had named the record alone, `cannot use '+' with Pick and int`
--- (Rosetta Code, Monads/List monad; Vijay, 2026-10-29)

struct Pick [x, y]

fn first[x]
    return x

log[first[5] + 1]
log[first[Pick[1, 2]].y]
